From: Timepiece Project
Subject: [PATCH] Verso: annotate sub-parts array to fix stuck genre metavariable

`FinishedPart.toSyntax` already annotates each block with `(b : Block genre)`
to work around a limitation in Lean's list/array elaboration: when an array
literal is "chunked", the intermediate let-bindings may fail to infer their
type. The sub-parts array was left unannotated, so for a manual with many
included chapters (~26) the chunked sub-parts let-bindings leave the implicit
genre of nested parts unresolved. A nested part's metadata then elaborates
against `PartMetadata ?m` with `?m` stuck, producing the hard error:

    invalid {...} notation, expected type is not of the form (C ...)
      Verso.Doc.Genre.PartMetadata ?m

Annotate the sub-parts with `(s : Part genre)`, mirroring the existing block
annotation. This lets the root `#doc` of the Timepiece book (26 included
chapters) elaborate and the single-page HTML to build.

Applies to verso v4.28.0 (commit 372f82ee4e67c863cf473a9174a1a77e0bec74a2).

--- a/src/verso/Verso/Doc/Elab/Basic.lean
+++ b/src/verso/Verso/Doc/Elab/Basic.lean
@@ -40,7 +40,11 @@ public partial def FinishedPart.toSyntax [Monad m] [MonadQuotation m]
     -- Adding type annotations works around a limitation in list and array elaboration, where intermediate
     -- let bindings introduced by "chunking" the elaboration may fail to infer types
     let typedBlocks ← blocks.mapM fun b => `(($b : Block $genre))
-    ``(Part.mk #[$titleInlines,*] $(quote titleString) $metaStx #[$typedBlocks,*] #[$subStx,*])
+    -- The sub-parts array must be annotated for the same reason: without the annotation, chunking
+    -- leaves the implicit genre of nested parts unresolved, so their metadata elaborates against a
+    -- stuck `PartMetadata ?m` (this surfaces as a hard error once a manual has ~26 included chapters).
+    let typedSubParts ← subStx.mapM fun s => `(($s : Part $genre))
+    ``(Part.mk #[$titleInlines,*] $(quote titleString) $metaStx #[$typedBlocks,*] #[$typedSubParts,*])
   | .included name => ``(VersoDoc.toPart $name)
 
 public partial def FinishedPart.toTOC : FinishedPart → TOC
